/simulation/rr/
inputs/**/*.csvy
!inputs/RR/**/*.csvy
inputs/**/*.qs
inputs/**/*.csv
inputs/**/*.fst
inputs/**/*.pdf
inputs/**/*.html
inputs/**/*.txt

# graphify knowledge graph: ENTIRELY ignored, outputs included.
#
# These files used to be tracked, on the reasoning that the human/AI-readable
# outputs were worth versioning. In practice that made them a constant source
# of spurious diffs: the graphify hook regenerates GRAPH_REPORT.md, graph.json,
# graph.html and manifest.json on every commit AND on every branch switch, so
# the working tree was dirty again the instant any git operation finished. A
# brand-new `git worktree add` came up with four modified files and a ~10,000
# line diff in graph.json.
#
# That is not cosmetic. `git rebase` and `git merge` both refuse to start on a
# dirty tree, so a regenerated artefact blocked them outright, and mid-rebase it
# conflicted on nearly every replayed commit (graph.json alone produced 206
# conflict hunks) — for a file whose "resolution" is always just to regenerate
# it. Together with the CRLF problem this is what made the repo unrebasable.
#
# Nothing is lost: the graph is a pure function of the source, rebuilt by
# `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost), and the hook rebuilds it
# automatically anyway. Regenerate rather than retrieve.
graphify-out/